WEBVTT

00:00:32.991 --> 00:00:35.536
Fry, I know those cookies
are fresh-a-licious,

00:00:35.619 --> 00:00:37.538
but they produce an awful lot of trash.

00:00:52.094 --> 00:00:55.722
And, Bender, that aerosol head spray
makes your antenna smell nice.

00:00:55.806 --> 00:00:56.890
- Thank you.
- But it's doing

00:00:56.974 --> 00:00:58.767
long-term damage to the planet.

00:00:58.851 --> 00:01:01.603
So? It's not like
it's the only one we've got.

00:01:02.145 --> 00:01:03.647
Good news, everyone.

00:01:03.730 --> 00:01:07.609
I'm sending you
on an extremely controversial mission.

00:01:07.658 --> 00:01:08.777
Controversial?

00:01:08.861 --> 00:01:10.362
Oh, my, no.

00:01:11.572 --> 00:01:13.907
For this highly controversial mission,

00:01:13.991 --> 00:01:16.326
you'll be towing the Juan Valdez,

00:01:16.410 --> 00:01:20.747
an orbiting supertanker
full of rich Colombian dark matter.

00:01:20.831 --> 00:01:22.040
Dark matter oil?

00:01:22.124 --> 00:01:24.334
What if we hit something?
The tanker could leak.

00:01:24.418 --> 00:01:25.961
Impossible.

00:01:26.044 --> 00:01:28.422
The tanker has 6,000 hulls.

00:01:28.505 --> 00:01:31.592
So, unlike me, it's entirely leakproof.

00:01:32.801 --> 00:01:36.555
Now, once you've hauled
the tanker past the protesters...

00:01:36.638 --> 00:01:38.557
- Protesters?
- Correct.

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:40.434
Six thousand hulls.

00:01:40.517 --> 00:01:44.563
Why do we have to fly within three feet
of this penguin preserve on Pluto?

00:01:44.646 --> 00:01:46.732
To avoid the tollbooth.

00:01:48.317 --> 00:01:51.945
Okay, she's all restocked
with emergency jam. Let's get going.

00:01:52.029 --> 00:01:54.198
At the risk of sounding negative, no.

00:01:54.281 --> 00:01:57.534
Look, Professor,
I can't participate in this mission.

00:01:57.618 --> 00:01:59.036
What are you yapping about?

00:01:59.119 --> 00:02:02.289
This time it's your reckless disregard
for the environment.

00:02:02.372 --> 00:02:05.292
In fact, I'm gonna
go join those protesters.

00:02:05.375 --> 00:02:07.044
This is an outrage!

00:02:07.127 --> 00:02:10.297
I demand you hand over
your captain's jacket.

00:02:10.380 --> 00:02:12.049
This is my normal jacket.

00:02:12.132 --> 00:02:13.550
I've had it for 10 years.

00:02:13.634 --> 00:02:14.885
I said hand it over.

00:02:16.678 --> 00:02:20.307
Well, Fry, or should I say

00:02:20.390 --> 00:02:22.059
Captain Fry?

00:02:22.142 --> 00:02:23.477
No, I shouldn't,

00:02:23.560 --> 00:02:25.979
because Bender is the new captain.

00:02:26.063 --> 00:02:27.898
- Bender?
- That's right.

00:02:27.981 --> 00:02:31.068
Being captain
is about intuition and heart.

00:02:31.151 --> 00:02:33.320
A good captain can't have either one.

00:02:33.403 --> 00:02:37.407
That's why cold, logical Bender
is perfect for the job.

00:02:37.491 --> 00:02:40.702
Well, I do think of human life
as expendable.

00:02:40.786 --> 00:02:42.079
No fair.

00:02:42.162 --> 00:02:44.122
Leela was training me to be captain.

00:02:44.206 --> 00:02:46.333
She even let me sit on her lap and steer,

00:02:46.416 --> 00:02:47.584
in this comic I drew.

00:02:47.668 --> 00:02:49.586
Ooh. The new one's out.

00:02:50.212 --> 00:02:53.674
Fry, the title of captain
may inflate the human ego,

00:02:53.757 --> 00:02:56.885
but it's beneath the notice
of my mighty robo-logic.

00:02:58.303 --> 00:02:59.555
Now, look spry, men!

00:02:59.638 --> 00:03:01.390
We launch at six bells.

00:03:12.192 --> 00:03:13.944
Greetings, eco-nauts.

00:03:14.027 --> 00:03:15.612
I'm Free Waterfall, Sr.,

00:03:15.696 --> 00:03:17.489
founder of Penguins Unlimited.

00:03:18.448 --> 00:03:21.285
No, no. No applause.

00:03:21.368 --> 00:03:24.872
Every time you clap your hands,
you kill thousands of spores

00:03:24.955 --> 00:03:27.207
that'll someday form a nutritious fungus.

00:03:27.291 --> 00:03:30.002
Just show your approval
with a mold-friendly thumbs up.

00:03:31.545 --> 00:03:33.797
Please hold your thumbs until the end.

00:03:33.881 --> 00:03:36.466
Now, folks, it's time to stop that tanker

00:03:36.550 --> 00:03:38.844
with a nonviolent human circle.

00:03:38.927 --> 00:03:41.013
Why do we have to resort to nonviolence?

00:03:41.096 --> 00:03:42.556
Can't we just kick their asses?

00:03:42.639 --> 00:03:43.807
Now, little lady,

00:03:43.891 --> 00:03:46.476
those people's asses
are living things, too.

00:03:52.065 --> 00:03:55.402
Aye! We're hitched up tighter
than Davy Jones's U-Haul.

00:03:55.485 --> 00:03:56.570
At ease, men.

00:03:57.070 --> 00:03:58.071
I am at ease.

00:03:58.155 --> 00:04:01.742
Mr. Fry, I like to give my first mate
an informal nickname.

00:04:01.825 --> 00:04:05.412
From now on, you'll be known as Wiggles.

00:04:05.495 --> 00:04:06.830
The hell I will!

00:04:06.914 --> 00:04:08.665
Have you even read the Captain's Handbook?

00:04:10.459 --> 00:04:11.502
I have now.

00:04:11.585 --> 00:04:14.421
And what's Peter Parrot's
first rule of captaining?

00:04:14.505 --> 00:04:17.966
Always respect the chain
o' command, Captain.

00:04:18.050 --> 00:04:19.343
Correct, Wiggles.

00:04:19.426 --> 00:04:22.679
You've just earned an invitation
to the captain's table.

00:04:24.181 --> 00:04:25.933
The captain's table.

00:04:26.016 --> 00:04:27.559
What an honor.

00:04:29.269 --> 00:04:32.731
Our peace ring has them trapped
like a tiger in a washing machine.

00:04:36.318 --> 00:04:37.319
Get ready!

00:04:37.402 --> 00:04:39.363
Okay, watch yourself. Here they come.

00:04:43.700 --> 00:04:45.661
When you were planning this peace ring,

00:04:45.744 --> 00:04:48.830
didn't you realize spaceships
can move in three dimensions?

00:04:48.914 --> 00:04:49.998
No, I did not.

00:05:00.259 --> 00:05:02.594
Folks, that tanker gave us the slip.

00:05:02.678 --> 00:05:04.721
But we'll stop them here on Pluto.

00:05:04.805 --> 00:05:07.349
If you're cold,
rub your bodies with permafrost.

00:05:07.432 --> 00:05:08.934
It's nature's long johns.

00:05:11.019 --> 00:05:14.648
If rubbing frozen dirt in your crotch
is wrong, hey, I don't wanna be right.

00:05:15.607 --> 00:05:17.609
This here is our penguin preserve.

00:05:19.528 --> 00:05:21.864
Aw. They're so cute.

00:05:21.947 --> 00:05:24.658
They're like if puppies
and kittens could have babies.

00:05:24.741 --> 00:05:28.370
We use hand puppets around the young'uns
to simulate a natural environment.

00:05:35.043 --> 00:05:37.296
That's adorable.

00:05:37.421 --> 00:05:38.505
Ow!

00:05:42.593 --> 00:05:45.721
But I suppose it's this medal
I'm most proud of, Wiggles.

00:05:45.804 --> 00:05:49.433
I won it for saving the children
of Earth from a giant kangaroo.

00:05:49.516 --> 00:05:52.269
It was on the Australian news.
You probably didn't see it.

00:05:52.352 --> 00:05:53.729
Brilliant!

00:05:53.812 --> 00:05:55.522
Would you cram a sock in it, Bender!

00:05:55.606 --> 00:05:56.773
Those aren't even medals.

00:05:56.857 --> 00:05:59.234
They're bottle caps and pepperoni slices.

00:06:01.612 --> 00:06:02.905
Thank you, steward.

00:06:02.988 --> 00:06:05.199
Wiggles, weren't you
about to propose a toast

00:06:05.282 --> 00:06:06.617
to your gallant captain?

00:06:06.700 --> 00:06:08.202
Fine! I've got a toast.

00:06:08.285 --> 00:06:10.579
To Captain Bender, he's the best...

00:06:11.330 --> 00:06:13.123
...at being a big jerk who's stupid,

00:06:13.207 --> 00:06:15.709
and his big ugly face
is as dumb as a butt.

00:06:16.043 --> 00:06:17.503
Ah, I've heard better.

00:06:17.586 --> 00:06:19.713
If I were in charge,
I wouldn't treat you like this.

00:06:19.796 --> 00:06:21.840
You're nothing but a big blowhard.

00:06:24.009 --> 00:06:26.136
Sir, you forget yourself!

00:06:26.220 --> 00:06:27.221
Shut up!

00:06:32.601 --> 00:06:34.811
Being captain is obviously
more important to you

00:06:34.895 --> 00:06:36.438
than being my friend.

00:06:36.522 --> 00:06:38.857
- I'm going.
- Going?

00:06:38.941 --> 00:06:42.152
But a captain can't drink
without his first mate.

00:06:45.822 --> 00:06:47.533
You can drink with me, maybe?

00:06:48.200 --> 00:06:49.743
I don't feel like drinking.

00:06:49.826 --> 00:06:52.704
Then if you'll excuse me,
I see some ravioli

00:06:52.788 --> 00:06:55.123
that only has two shoe prints on it.

00:06:55.415 --> 00:06:57.000
Three.

00:07:04.508 --> 00:07:07.594
Oh, Greenland is a barren land

00:07:07.678 --> 00:07:10.556
A land that bears no green

00:07:10.639 --> 00:07:14.601
Where there's ice and snow
And the whalefishies blow

00:07:14.685 --> 00:07:16.979
Captain, please, have some liquor.

00:07:17.062 --> 00:07:19.314
You robots need alcohol to function.

00:07:19.398 --> 00:07:22.192
Get out! I once knew a guy.

00:07:22.276 --> 00:07:23.569
You look like him.

00:07:23.652 --> 00:07:25.279
He wasn't neither.

00:07:26.613 --> 00:07:28.365
I'm a good captain.

00:07:28.448 --> 00:07:31.159
Please, sir. I love you like a father.

00:07:37.249 --> 00:07:38.250
Here they come.

00:07:38.333 --> 00:07:39.835
Oh, I hope they read my sign.

00:07:43.380 --> 00:07:45.174
Bender's flying too low!

00:07:45.257 --> 00:07:46.675
And he's upside down!

00:07:46.758 --> 00:07:48.510
He must be talking on a cell phone.

00:08:00.230 --> 00:08:01.273
What's happening?

00:08:02.232 --> 00:08:05.194
All 6,000 hulls have been breached!

00:08:05.277 --> 00:08:06.820
Oh, the fools!

00:08:06.904 --> 00:08:09.740
If only they'd built it with 6,001 hulls.

00:08:09.823 --> 00:08:11.325
When will they learn?

00:08:25.005 --> 00:08:29.134
Continuing our coverage
of a tragic, but faraway, story.

00:08:29.218 --> 00:08:31.053
The crisis on Pluto worsens

00:08:31.136 --> 00:08:33.931
as dark matter spreads
throughout the penguin habitat.

00:08:34.014 --> 00:08:36.141
The images are truly horrific.

00:08:43.273 --> 00:08:45.359
I don't think any of us can understand

00:08:45.442 --> 00:08:48.320
how those poor,
oil-drenched penguins feel.

00:08:50.906 --> 00:08:52.616
Oily humanoid.

00:08:54.701 --> 00:08:57.204
At the time of the crash,
the tanker captain

00:08:57.287 --> 00:08:59.998
had an alcohol level of .08%,

00:09:00.082 --> 00:09:03.001
well below the legal limit for robots.

00:09:04.628 --> 00:09:06.505
Son, as your lawyer,

00:09:06.588 --> 00:09:10.092
I declare y'all are in
a 12-piece bucket of trouble.

00:09:10.175 --> 00:09:12.094
But I done struck you a deal.

00:09:12.177 --> 00:09:14.388
Five hours of community service

00:09:14.471 --> 00:09:16.473
cleaning up that whole mess you caused.

00:09:16.557 --> 00:09:18.851
Five hours? Oh, man!

00:09:18.934 --> 00:09:20.936
Couldn't you have just got me
the death penalty?

00:09:21.019 --> 00:09:23.647
I'd have done better, but it's plumb hard

00:09:23.730 --> 00:09:27.860
pleading a case while awaiting trial
for that there incompetence.

00:09:27.943 --> 00:09:29.695
Yeah, good luck with that.

00:09:48.422 --> 00:09:50.966
Now you stay away from those puffin twins.

00:09:53.218 --> 00:09:55.220
Good way to avoid frostbite, folks,

00:09:55.304 --> 00:09:57.681
put your hands between your buttocks.

00:09:57.764 --> 00:09:59.224
That's nature's pocket.

00:09:59.308 --> 00:10:01.894
Uh... I think I'll go check on Bender.

00:10:01.977 --> 00:10:03.770
Watch that he doesn't pick your pocket.

00:10:08.859 --> 00:10:10.527
Can't beat fresh-squeezed.

00:10:10.611 --> 00:10:13.947
Bender, can you at least pretend
you're being punished?

00:10:16.408 --> 00:10:18.410
And clean the black parts, too.

00:10:20.704 --> 00:10:23.498
Are they black with white feathers
or white with black feathers?

00:10:23.582 --> 00:10:26.668
It don't matter, baby.
They're all beautiful.

00:10:28.462 --> 00:10:30.756
Yo, screws, more Tegrin over here.

00:10:31.215 --> 00:10:32.716
Oh! What's this?

00:10:51.693 --> 00:10:53.570
Oh, man, he got away.

00:10:53.654 --> 00:10:55.948
I guess this is why Chief says no hugging.

00:10:58.158 --> 00:10:59.451
Good work, everyone.

00:10:59.535 --> 00:11:01.703
I suggest you all go get some sleep.

00:11:01.787 --> 00:11:04.122
Me? Well, I'm gonna stay up all night

00:11:04.206 --> 00:11:07.251
singing songs about penguins
in a fine, piercing tenor.

00:11:08.794 --> 00:11:10.128
Has anyone seen Bender?

00:11:10.754 --> 00:11:12.381
Bender!

00:11:12.464 --> 00:11:14.633
Here, robot, robot, robot!

00:11:16.552 --> 00:11:19.638
Hey, why weren't you Kong Donkeys
outside cleaning up?

00:11:19.721 --> 00:11:23.517
They sent us inside
for doing an unsatisfactory job,

00:11:23.600 --> 00:11:25.561
and eating penguin eggs.

00:11:25.644 --> 00:11:26.937
You ate most of them.

00:11:27.437 --> 00:11:29.231
So, where's Captain Bender?

00:11:29.314 --> 00:11:31.358
Off catastrophizing some other planet?

00:11:33.068 --> 00:11:34.069
Damn it, Fry!

00:11:34.152 --> 00:11:36.446
He may have done wrong,
but he's still your captain.

00:11:36.530 --> 00:11:39.032
I'm worried about him.
He didn't come back with the group.

00:11:39.116 --> 00:11:40.492
- He didn't?
- No.

00:11:40.576 --> 00:11:43.495
And with windchill
it's 20 degrees below absolute zero.

00:11:43.579 --> 00:11:44.580
I better go find him.

00:11:44.663 --> 00:11:45.914
Wait. Let me.

00:11:45.998 --> 00:11:47.749
Bender and I have our disagreements,

00:11:47.833 --> 00:11:49.084
but we're still friends.

00:11:49.168 --> 00:11:51.170
And I'm gonna show him what that means.

00:11:54.131 --> 00:11:55.174
To the ship!

00:11:55.257 --> 00:11:56.633
Why don't you just walk?

00:11:56.717 --> 00:11:59.011
He was only about 20 yards from here.

00:11:59.094 --> 00:12:01.180
Madam, I am in command now.

00:12:01.722 --> 00:12:03.182
Such a man.

00:12:03.265 --> 00:12:06.018
I'd follow him to hell and back, I would.

00:12:19.573 --> 00:12:21.700
What the...

00:12:26.079 --> 00:12:28.123
What's this water made of, ice?

00:12:28.207 --> 00:12:29.541
Forget this!

00:13:13.752 --> 00:13:16.046
Captain, I don't think
we're on Pluto any longer.

00:13:16.129 --> 00:13:18.590
In fact, we may have
left space as we know it.

00:13:18.674 --> 00:13:19.925
Then where are we?

00:13:20.008 --> 00:13:21.718
You said you knew how to navigate.

00:13:21.802 --> 00:13:24.596
Stop yelling at me!

00:14:41.106 --> 00:14:42.941
Folks, it's worse than we thought.

00:14:43.025 --> 00:14:46.361
Seems dark matter is nature's sex drug.

00:14:46.445 --> 00:14:50.198
It's like a perverted
trail mix of penguin estrogen,

00:14:50.282 --> 00:14:52.993
penguin Viagra and Spanish penguin fly.

00:14:53.076 --> 00:14:54.578
Why, it's making them ultra-fertile.

00:14:54.661 --> 00:14:55.662
How ultra?

00:14:55.746 --> 00:14:59.041
Well, your garden variety penguin
lays one egg a year.

00:14:59.124 --> 00:15:01.877
Since the spill, our penguins
have been laying six eggs

00:15:01.960 --> 00:15:03.920
every 15 minutes.

00:15:04.004 --> 00:15:06.173
Also, the eggs hatch in only 12 hours.

00:15:07.257 --> 00:15:09.051
Also, the males are laying eggs.

00:15:12.262 --> 00:15:13.680
This man has over-gasped.

00:15:15.557 --> 00:15:18.685
If the birds keep multiplying,
there'll soon be too many to count.

00:15:19.144 --> 00:15:22.147
Before long, the penguins
will exhaust their food supply

00:15:22.230 --> 00:15:23.857
and starve to death.

00:15:24.691 --> 00:15:27.402
Oh, if only we hadn't flown penguins
to Pluto

00:15:27.486 --> 00:15:30.113
and dumped oil on them,
this might never have happened.

00:15:30.197 --> 00:15:32.115
Can't we stop them from multiplying?

00:15:32.199 --> 00:15:34.785
Yes, I reckon it is our responsibility.

00:15:34.868 --> 00:15:36.328
And thankfully, we have a plan.

00:15:36.411 --> 00:15:38.163
What is it? We'll do anything.

00:15:38.246 --> 00:15:40.457
Everyone, grab your guns.

00:15:40.540 --> 00:15:43.835
I declare penguin-hunting season
officially open!

00:15:52.502 --> 00:15:53.962
We can't shoot penguins!

00:15:54.046 --> 00:15:56.423
Isn't there some way
to keep them from breeding?

00:15:56.506 --> 00:15:59.718
Cold showers don't work
on Antarctic creatures.

00:15:59.801 --> 00:16:02.679
Now, surely you agree
that a quick semi-painless death

00:16:02.763 --> 00:16:04.932
is a damn sight better
than weeks of starvation.

00:16:05.015 --> 00:16:08.477
Well, I suppose, but... I mean,

00:16:08.560 --> 00:16:12.272
I joined Penguins Unlimited
to love penguins, not to hunt them.

00:16:12.356 --> 00:16:14.441
This time, the two are one and the same.

00:16:14.524 --> 00:16:15.609
Now, are you with us,

00:16:15.692 --> 00:16:17.945
or are you gonna let
innocent penguins suffer?

00:16:20.489 --> 00:16:22.532
Oh, God, it's inhuman!

00:16:22.616 --> 00:16:24.159
It's like Hong Kong!

00:16:24.493 --> 00:16:25.494
I'll do it!

00:16:26.578 --> 00:16:30.040
That's a good old-fashioned gun.
Simple point-and-click interface.

00:16:30.499 --> 00:16:32.793
- Rifle check!
- Oh, yeah!

00:16:32.876 --> 00:16:34.211
Wee doggie!

00:16:34.503 --> 00:16:36.672
Hey, you're enjoying this.

00:16:36.755 --> 00:16:39.258
Look, nobody enjoys shooting penguins.

00:16:39.341 --> 00:16:42.302
But if you have to shoot penguins,
well, you might as well enjoy it.

00:16:42.761 --> 00:16:43.762
I'm sorry,

00:16:43.845 --> 00:16:46.765
but if it's fun in any way,
it's not environmentalism.

00:16:46.848 --> 00:16:49.184
Oh, really? How about blowing up dams?

00:16:49.685 --> 00:16:51.812
Yeah, that is fun.

00:16:51.895 --> 00:16:53.814
Let's conservate.

00:16:57.568 --> 00:17:00.612
It's been an honor
to serve under you, sir.

00:17:07.411 --> 00:17:10.080
All right. This is for their own good.

00:17:10.163 --> 00:17:13.208
Don't leave orphans.
Gotta kill entire families.

00:17:17.838 --> 00:17:19.965
But they're so cute.

00:17:20.048 --> 00:17:21.675
No, you can do this.

00:17:21.758 --> 00:17:23.927
It's just like murdering a little butler.

00:17:24.761 --> 00:17:26.972
I... I can't look.

00:17:32.603 --> 00:17:34.062
Oh, no!

00:17:34.605 --> 00:17:35.981
What have I done?

00:17:41.069 --> 00:17:43.280
You poor little guy!

00:17:43.363 --> 00:17:44.823
I'm so sorry.

00:17:44.907 --> 00:17:45.991
I... Bender?

00:17:54.791 --> 00:17:55.918
What's going on?

00:17:56.001 --> 00:17:57.878
Were you hiding out
with these little guys?

00:17:57.961 --> 00:17:59.087
Of course not!

00:17:59.171 --> 00:18:00.464
Filthy ice rats.

00:18:00.547 --> 00:18:01.840
Scat! Shoo!

00:18:03.175 --> 00:18:04.927
What are you doing? Get away.

00:18:05.302 --> 00:18:07.137
Aw! They love you.

00:18:07.221 --> 00:18:08.639
Well, I don't love them.

00:18:09.389 --> 00:18:10.849
Aw.

00:18:14.978 --> 00:18:16.480
I don't know why,

00:18:16.563 --> 00:18:18.690
but when I look down
at their little faces,

00:18:18.774 --> 00:18:20.317
it makes me wanna puke.

00:18:20.400 --> 00:18:21.485
In a good way.

00:18:33.205 --> 00:18:34.831
Stop! Stop shooting!

00:18:35.457 --> 00:18:37.084
It's me, Leela.

00:18:37.167 --> 00:18:38.460
Sorry.

00:18:38.919 --> 00:18:41.546
Why aren't you firing randomly
into those birds, little lady?

00:18:41.630 --> 00:18:42.881
Don't you wanna help them?

00:18:42.965 --> 00:18:43.966
Not this way.

00:18:44.049 --> 00:18:45.050
What?

00:18:45.133 --> 00:18:47.636
Why, you're not
a tree-hugging kook at all.

00:18:47.719 --> 00:18:51.473
Look, I don't know if shooting penguins
will help the environment or not,

00:18:51.557 --> 00:18:54.518
but I do know the decision
shouldn't be in the hands of people

00:18:54.601 --> 00:18:56.520
who just wanna kill for fun.

00:18:57.396 --> 00:19:01.233
Leela, you may just be farming
some free-range truth there.

00:19:02.359 --> 00:19:06.113
On the other hand, we already made up
200 pounds of batter for penguin tempura.

00:19:06.196 --> 00:19:08.490
Okay, boys, it's them or us!

00:19:09.032 --> 00:19:10.242
No!

00:19:11.368 --> 00:19:13.453
- Hey, where'd they...
- Attack!

00:19:26.466 --> 00:19:28.010
Oh, God.

00:19:30.554 --> 00:19:33.974
Make sure they use every part of my body!

00:19:34.057 --> 00:19:36.435
I'll avenge your death, son!

00:19:37.019 --> 00:19:39.187
They used to be such peaceful birds.

00:19:39.271 --> 00:19:40.898
I suppose this was your doing.

00:19:40.981 --> 00:19:42.482
Yep, it's like I taught them.

00:19:42.566 --> 00:19:45.569
If it ain't black and white,
peck, scratch and bite.

00:19:45.652 --> 00:19:47.613
Now, to take off my tuxedo.

00:19:52.618 --> 00:19:55.621
Guys, it's me, your lovable dictator.
Uh-oh.

00:20:02.461 --> 00:20:05.422
Oh. If only we had a toboggan.

00:20:08.216 --> 00:20:09.551
Faster! Faster!

00:20:26.318 --> 00:20:28.153
Oh, right, they can swim.

00:20:28.237 --> 00:20:29.529
It's all coming back to me now.

00:20:35.994 --> 00:20:37.871
- It's Fry.
- Wiggles?

00:20:45.712 --> 00:20:49.007
Well, at least it'll help
reduce their population.

00:20:49.091 --> 00:20:52.135
Yeah, life is hilariously cruel.

00:20:58.642 --> 00:21:00.435
Permission to come aboard, Wiggles?

00:21:00.519 --> 00:21:03.814
Granted. We can't take off
without our captain.

00:21:07.025 --> 00:21:09.319
Oh, and bring my toboggan.

00:21:12.781 --> 00:21:15.033
So, Leela, were you able
to help the penguins?

00:21:15.117 --> 00:21:16.118
Well, sure.

00:21:16.201 --> 00:21:17.869
I mean, not really.

00:21:17.953 --> 00:21:20.497
I mean, nature will work itself out.

00:21:20.581 --> 00:21:22.583
It can't screw things up
any worse than we did

00:21:22.666 --> 00:21:24.251
trying to fix things. Right?

00:21:24.334 --> 00:21:26.753
- I don't know.
- Quit your worrying.

00:21:26.837 --> 00:21:28.797
Thanks to my shining influence,

00:21:28.880 --> 00:21:32.050
those stupid birds will do just fine.